ai_response:
Under Section 7(1) of the Right to Information Act, 2005, I am providing the response as follows:

**Section Citation**: Under Section 4(1)(b) of the RTI Act, 2005.

**Contextual Source**: [Source: rti_act_2005.pdf, Page: 5]

**Reasoning**: As per Section 4(1)(b) of the RTI Act, every public authority is obligated to publish the following categories of information proactively:

**Information/Refusal**: The categories of information that must be published proactively by every public authority are:

* (i) the particulars of facilities available to citizens for obtaining information, including the working hours of a library or reading room, if maintained for public use;
* (ii) the names, designations and other particulars of the Public Information Officers;
* (xvii) such other information as may be prescribed;

**Appeal Path**: If you are unsatisfied with this response, you may file a first appeal under Section 19(1) of the RTI Act, 2005 within 30 days to the First Appellate Authority (FAA) at FAA-Demo@gov.in.
